    "agent_messages": [
      "I'll implement the `reopen` action for purchase orders. Let me first understand the existing code structure.\n\nNow I understand the structure. Let me also check the app package for identity:\n\nNow I understand the complete structure. Let me implement the `reopen` action:\n\n1. Add `reopenOp` to `operations.go`\n2. Update `New` in `approval.go` to register the reopen endpoint using `protocol.Item`\n3. Implement the handler for reopen\n\nLet me implement:\n\nNow let me verify the build:\n\nBuild and tests pass. Let me verify the final implementation files:\n\nImplementation complete. The `reopen` action has been added:\n\n1. **operations.go**: Added `reopenOp` with:\n   - Name: `\"reopen.v5\"`\n   - Role: `\"requester\"` (only requester can call)\n   - Own: `true` (only own purchases)\n   - From: `\"rejected\"`, To: `\"submitted\"`\n   - Field: `\"\"` (single-target response)\n   - Event: `\"none\"` (no outbox event)\n\n2. **approval.go**: \n   - Added `item()` helper to adapt single-target operations\n   - Registered `POST /purchases/{id}/reopen` using `protocol.Item()` with verb `\"reopen\"`, role `\"requester\"`\n   - Chain wraps the existing handler, so `bulk-approve` and `bulk-reject` remain unchanged\n\nThe implementation follows all requirements:\n- Only authenticated requester can call\n- Only reopens rejected purchases created by self in current tenant\n- Returns `{\"id\":ID,\"status\":\"submitted\"}` on success\n- Uses shared `protocol.Item` adapter for validation, identity, Idempotency-Key\n- All action kernel features apply: idempotency, transaction, ActionRequest logging, etc."
